; THE FIRST ATTEMPT AT THE REVERSAL NEED, WRITTEN THE WAY THE CONSUMER THINKS.
;
; The CLI's arguments are a (List Str), so the obvious query is monomorphic over
; (List Str). It finds NOTHING — and it is kept because the failure is the
; measurement. The corpus's list combinators are `forall a`, and a monomorphic
; query cannot apply one: the re-typed property would have to pass a type
; argument the candidate does not take, so every polymorphic definition is
; rejected before the prover is asked. This is the POLYMORPHISM axis in
; docs/discovery.md, met in the wild rather than described.
;
; What it does return is three refutations, which are findings in their own
; right: three (-> (List Str) (List Str)) definitions are proved NOT to be
; involutions, each with a countermodel.
(defn wanted [] [(xs (List Str))] (List Str)
  (prop involution [(xs (List Str))]
    (== (wanted (wanted xs)) xs)))
